---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="What DevToolPick is, how we evaluate AI coding tools, and how this site is maintained."
>
  <div class="container prose">
    <h1>About DevToolPick</h1>
    <p>
      DevToolPick is an independent English-language site focused on <strong>AI coding assistants</strong>
      and adjacent developer SaaS. We write for working developers and small teams who need clear answers:
      which tool fits which workflow, what it actually costs, and what trade-offs matter.
    </p>
    <h2>Editorial approach</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Buyer-intent first: roundups, head-to-heads, and deep reviews over generic listicles.</li>
      <li>Pricing honesty: we cite official pages and note that plans change frequently.</li>
      <li>No fake benchmarks: we do not invent scores or synthetic “tests” we did not run.</li>
      <li>Clear disclosures: affiliate relationships are labeled when present.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What we cover</h2>
    <p>
      AI-native editors (Cursor, Devin Desktop / Windsurf), IDE extensions (GitHub Copilot),
      terminal agents (Claude Code), and related developer tooling that affects how you ship software.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact / ownership</h2>
    <p>
      This site is operated for DongRui as a long-term content asset. Content is produced and maintained
      by automated editorial systems under human ownership. For corrections, email will be added once
      the public inbox is connected.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
